Article 5
Every female victim of violence has: The right to have her dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. The right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. The right to determine her own decisions;
d. The right to obtain information;
e. The right to confidentiality;
f. The right to social rehabilitation;
g. The right to complaint handling;
h. The right of the victim and her family to obtain
i. facilities in the judicial process; and The right to assistance.

Article 9
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government in providing Protection for Women as referred to in Article 8 letter a include: establishing policies for the protection of women;
b. implementing policies, protection, of women from acts of violence in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. conducting protection cooperation in women;
d. providing ΠΑΓΩΤΑ infrastructure support for the protection of women;
e. allocating....13 -13-
e. allocating budget for protection empowerment implementation of women financial capacity of the Region; and
f. fostering and supervising the protection of women.
in accordance implementation (2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women in the Regional action plan as a basis for Regional Apparatus in implementing the protection of women.
(3) The Regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be included in the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.
(4) Further provisions regarding the Regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 29
(1) The guidance and supervision team as referred to in Article 27 paragraph (2) letter b shall be established by the Regent. (2) The team as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be led by the head of the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs under the authority of the Region in the field of women's empowerment.
(3) The team as referred to in paragraph (1) shall consist of at least: in the Regional Apparatus that has the duty to assist the Regent in policy formulation and administrative coordination of the implementation of regional apparatus duties as well as administrative services. b. Regional apparatus that has the duty to assist the Regent in guiding and supervising the implementation of governmental affairs under the authority of the Region and Co-Administration Tasks;
c. Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs under the authority of the Region in the field of health;
d. Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs under the authority of the Region in the field of social affairs;
e. Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs under the authority of the Region in the field of public order;
f. Prosecutor's Office....24 -24-
f. Prosecutor's Office of the Republic of Indonesia;
g. Police of the Republic of Indonesia; and
h. UPTD PPA.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
(1) The Regional Government organizes the Protection of Women from violence.
